# Copy this file to .env.scripts. Make loads it before running supported tools
# in scripts/. Keep .env.scripts local: it may eventually contain credentials.

# Vision Bill API used by scripts/create_benchmark_run.py and by
# scripts/context_budget.py when it reads the current tag vocabulary.
VB_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
VB_APP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
# API benchmarks require an admin, explicit --model selections and current Gold
# qualified by a human. Keep credentials in the ignored .env.scripts file.
# VB_USERNAME=admin
# VB_PASSWORD=

# The context-budget diagnostic uses the Ollama API.
# OLLAMA_HOST=http://127.0.0.1:11434
# The standalone benchmark uses the loaded application LLM settings, including
# LLM__PROVIDER, LLM__HOST, LLM__MODEL_NAME, LLM__API_KEY and LLM__TEMPERATURE.
# Set these for your selected provider, endpoint and model. An explicit
# --llm-host or --model overrides its corresponding field.
# For managed native OCR, match the app's provider, LLM__MODEL_LIFECYCLE and
# exact LLM__HOST spelling. For the context-budget diagnostic, match OLLAMA_HOST.
# See OPENAI_COMPATIBLE.md for a dedicated llama.cpp router.
# Match the production OCR settings and the actual coordination volume or bind mount.
# Production selection: canonical endpoint overrides legacy enabled/service_url;
# absence preserves legacy. Keep production OCR selected for managed ownership.
# OCR__ENDPOINT=http://your-explicitly-exposed-local-sidecar:8082
# Both manual CLIs (standalone_benchmark.py and test_ocr_service.py) overwrite
# their URL using --ocr-url > OCR__SERVICE_URL > http://localhost:8082.
# OCR__ENDPOINT alone does not supply their URL. Set the matching URL below or
# pass --ocr-url; both selections must identify the same intended managed service.
# OCR__SERVICE_URL=http://your-explicitly-exposed-local-sidecar:8082
# OCR-only bundles must use OCR_SERVICE_MODE=managed when paired with VisionBill.
# The CUDA/ROCm activation overlays mount the project's ocr-coordination volume
# at /coord. A CLI sharing that mount and deployment uses the same lock path:
# OCR__COORDINATION_PATH=/coord/gpu-handoff.lock
# For separately configured OCR use the installation's actual coordination path.
# Preserve endpoint spelling across processes: journal identity binds LLM__HOST.

# Optional PostgreSQL overrides for context_budget.py --db-sample.
# Base Compose publishes no host DB port. Set an explicitly reachable endpoint;
# 5432 below is illustrative, not an automatic port mapping.
PG__USER=vision_bill
PG__PASSWORD=vision_bill
PG__DB=vision_bill
PG__HOST=127.0.0.1
PG__PORT=5432

# Owner/migration connection used only by `make db-configure-roles`. Keep the
# password in .env.scripts, never in this tracked example.
# MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://migration_owner@127.0.0.1:5432/vision_bill
# Bootstrap missing privilege groups as admin/CREATEROLE, then run grants as owner.
# Alembic uses PG__*; this URL is not an entrypoint migration credential override.
# Standalone benchmark additionally requires --user-id for one real owner and
# SELECT-only credentials. context_budget --db-sample only reads existing images.
